{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29444 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "Laxanthone-I is implicated in the regulation of the High-affinity choline transporter through a series of molecular interactions. The drug acts as a target of multiple enzymes, including the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is itself a target of other compounds such as 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide and Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate. These intermediates, in turn, are linked to the High-affinity choline transporter, suggesting a potential pathway where Laxanthone-I influences the activity of these enzymes, which in turn modulate the transporter's function. The evidence suggests that Laxanthone-I may exert its effects by interacting with or regulating the activity of enzymes that ultimately influence the choline transporter, though the exact mechanism of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple indirect pathways supports the idea that Laxanthone-I could be a modulator of the choline transporter, potentially through a complex network of enzymatic interactions.",
